@startuml
title Attack Tree - Data Compromise through Input Injection

skinparam backgroundColor #f4f4f4
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam rectangle {
	BorderColor #5c5c5c
	FontColor #1f1f1f
	RoundCorner 8
}

rectangle "Attacker compromises data\nthrough input injection" as ROOT #e6f7ff

rectangle "Attacker submits SQL injection\npayloads in search/filter inputs" as SQLI #ffffff
rectangle "Attacker submits stored script\nin game metadata" as XSS #ffffff
rectangle "Attacker pollutes external\nmetadata ingestion flow" as POLLUTION #ffffff

rectangle "Mitigate with strict server-side\ninput validation and\nparameterized query patterns" as M_SQLI #d6f5ea
rectangle "Mitigate with output encoding,\ncontent sanitization, and\nauthenticated endpoint checks" as M_XSS #d6f5ea
rectangle "Mitigate with validation gates for\nexternal data and dependency hygiene" as M_POLLUTION #d6f5ea

ROOT -down-> SQLI
ROOT -down-> XSS
ROOT -down-> POLLUTION

SQLI -down-> M_SQLI
XSS -down-> M_XSS
POLLUTION -down-> M_POLLUTION

note bottom
Attack path logic:
- Branches from ROOT are OR alternatives.
- Each mitigation block defines the primary defensive response for that branch.
end note

@enduml
